I cannot justify either a categorical “yes” or a universal “no.” The current residual has a provable first-move obstruction; an information-based decomposition can avoid that identity and has a useful theoretical conditioning bound. But the available facts do not establish that three such sources contain distinct, decision-relevant information or can deliver substantial pooled EE gains. The answer will leave that broader question open and specify what evidence would resolve it.
